# Offline-First Rules

## Driver app
The driver must be able to operate an already-synchronized delivery offline for documented actions such as:
- viewing delivery data;
- using available location/map data;
- recording arrival;
- confirming pickup;
- recording proof of delivery;
- recording failure;
- recording return actions when supported.

## Rules
- Persist critical offline actions locally before considering them safely recorded.
- Each offline mutation must have a stable client event/idempotency identifier.
- Never assume network availability.
- Never block an active delivery workflow simply because a sync attempt failed, provided the action is allowed offline.
- Clearly mark local pending changes.
- Do not create a new marketplace offer while offline in MVP.
- Do not fabricate server confirmation when only local persistence succeeded.
- When reconnecting, synchronize safely and reconcile authoritative responses.
